# Revisions to skip in `git blame` — mechanical reformatting only, no behaviour
# change. Without this, one whole-tree rewrite makes itself the author of every
# line it touched.
#
# Opt in locally (once per clone):
#
#   git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
#
# GitHub's blame view reads this file automatically; no setup needed there.
#
# One full 40-character SHA per line, newest last, with the commit subject in a
# comment above it. Add a commit here only when the blame it rescues clearly
# outweighs the blame it costs.
#
# Note on this repo's workflow: PRs are squash-merged into `develop`, so a
# feature branch's individual commits never reach `develop` and their SHAs are
# not valid here. The SHA to list is always the squashed commit as it landed.
# That means an entry can only be added *after* its PR merges, in a follow-up.
#
# A squashed normalization commit is necessarily not purely mechanical — it
# carries the policy and guard alongside the reformatting. That is an accepted
# trade: it rescues blame on the hundreds of reformatted files at the cost of a
# handful of lines in the few pre-existing files the same PR edited.

# (empty — the LF normalization SHA is added once #115 lands on develop; see
# docs/line-endings.md)
